    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d234">

                <pb facs="0753" n="729" sameAs="frus:frus1946v02/pg729"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/7–346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-03T14:00:00+01:00">July 3, 1946—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3270. For the Acting Secretary from the Secretary, Delsec 659. If agreement is
                    reached on reparations deliveries to the USSR from Italy out of current
                    production, it is my intention to propose that treaty provide for such
                    deliveries within definite limits, on the basis that the USSR would furnish the
                    necessary materials needed for the production of these goods by Italy. It is my
                    belief that the character of the goods to be supplied by Italy and of the
                    materials to be furnished by the <pb facs="0754" n="730" xml:id="pg730"/> USSR
                    should, within the limits set up by the treaty, be agreed upon between Italy and
                    the USSR.</p>
                <p>The communication which the Embassy at Rome was instructed to make to the Italian
                    Government in Deptel 1382 to Rome July 1 repeated to Paris as Secdel 385<anchor
                        n="27" xml:id="d234-f1"/> might be considered to be in conflict with the
                    proposals I have in mind, and I question the wisdom of making such a
                    communication to the Italian Government at this time.</p>
                <p>Sent to Department, repeated to Rome for the Chargé only as 175.</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
